course: dictionary
lesson: 3793
title: Small word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «for» is tiny, but it has many jobs. Look at the words that come after it to find its meaning. «A seat is for a person, so put your bag on your lap or the floor when the bus is busy.» Here «for» shows who the seat is meant for: a person, not a bag.
explain: Try the same check each time. «Mia bought a pen for 3 pounds» shows a price, because the pen costs 3 pounds. «Thanks for helping» shows a reason. «Older children need breakfast, sleep and time for themselves» shows that the time belongs to them. Ask: what does «for» point to?
explain: «Albino animals are easier for predators to spot.» Here «for» tells you whose view the word is about: the predators find it easier. When you read a sentence with «for», check the words after it, then swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «For» is most often a preposition, a word that links one thing to another, as in «a gift for Mum».
fact: «For» can show who something is meant for: «a seat is for a person».
fact: «For» can show how long something lasts: «for two hours», or a price: «a pen for 3 pounds».
fact: «For» can give a reason or purpose: «thanks for helping», «for fun».
fact: In casual talk, «for real» means «are you serious?» and «for ages» means a very long time.
exercise: «A seat is for a person, so put your bag on your lap or the floor when the bus is busy.» Who is the seat meant for? | The bus driver | A bag | *A person | The floor
exercise: Mia says, «I bought a pen for 3 pounds.» What does «for» show here? | Support for a team | *A price | A reason | A length of time
exercise: Ella asks, «Are you for or against the new park?» What does «for» mean here? | Far away from the park | *In support of the park | Before the park | Because of the park
test: «Albino animals often see poorly, burn easily in sun and are easier for predators to spot.» In the words «easier for predators to spot», who finds it easier? | *The predators | Both of them | The sun | The animals
test: Jayden says, «I've waited for ages!» What does «for ages» mean? | *A very long time | A price of a few pounds | In support of the team | Only for one person
exam: The club was open «for a period of four days». What does «for a period of» show? | Support for a cause | The person it is meant for | *How long something lasts | A price
